From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Fable 5.1" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sdhci: Auto CMD23 for multi-block in v4 mode

U-Boot issues every multi-block transfer open-ended: CMD18 with the
block count only in the host's own register, no CMD23 in front of it and
no auto command configured, then a CMD12 sent by hand afterwards. Linux
sends CMD23 for eMMC as a matter of course, and in Host Version 4 mode
SDHCI can issue it for you -- the count goes in the register at
SDHCI_32BIT_BLK_CNT, which doubles as the Auto CMD23 argument, and the
controller sends the command itself.

On Cadence SD4HC (Axera AX630C) an open-ended CMD18 never starts its
data phase: the card answers R1 from TRAN and drives nothing, ending in
DATA_TIMEOUT with no ADMA error, while CMD17 at the same address returns
its block. That holds in HS, HS200 and HS400ES, with ADMA2 32-bit and
96-bit descriptors, with SDMA and with PIO, and with Auto CMD12 -- every
combination the driver can produce. A closed-ended transfer is the one
thing left that has never been tried on it.

With the controller sending CMD23 the transfer is closed-ended and needs
no stop, so the core must not send one: CMD12 to a card the controller
has already returned to TRAN fails, and mmc_read_blocks() reads that as
a failed transfer.

Signed-off-by: open-nanokvm-pro contributors <nanokvm@localhost>
---
 drivers/mmc/mmc.c   | 2 +-
 drivers/mmc/sdhci.c | 9 ++++++++-
 include/mmc.h       | 2 ++
 include/sdhci.h     | 1 +
 4 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/sdhci.h b/include/sdhci.h
--- a/include/sdhci.h
+++ b/include/sdhci.h
@@ -35,2 +35,3 @@
 #define  SDHCI_TRNS_ACMD12	BIT(2)
+#define  SDHCI_TRNS_AUTO_CMD23	BIT(3)
 #define  SDHCI_TRNS_READ	BIT(4)
diff --git a/include/mmc.h b/include/mmc.h
--- a/include/mmc.h
+++ b/include/mmc.h
@@ -622,6 +622,8 @@
 	uint f_max;
 	uint b_max;
 	unsigned char part_type;
+	/* The host closes multi-block transfers itself; the core sends no CMD12. */
+	bool auto_stop;
 	/*
 	 * eMMC driver strength from "fixed-emmc-driver-type", as an eMMC
 	 * spec table-206 value shifted into place for EXT_CSD_HS_TIMING.
diff --git a/drivers/mmc/mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/mmc.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/mmc.c
@@ -483,3 +483,3 @@
 
-	if (blkcnt > 1) {
+	if (blkcnt > 1 && !mmc->cfg->auto_stop) {
 		if (mmc_send_stop_transmission(mmc, false)) {
diff --git a/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c b/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c
@@ -281,4 +281,10 @@
 		trans_bytes = data->blocks * data->blocksize;
-		if (data->blocks > 1)
+		if (data->blocks > 1) {
 			mode |= SDHCI_TRNS_MULTI | SDHCI_TRNS_BLK_CNT_EN;
+			if (host->v4_mode) {
+				mode |= SDHCI_TRNS_AUTO_CMD23;
+				sdhci_writel(host, data->blocks,
+					     SDHCI_32BIT_BLK_CNT);
+			}
+		}
 
diff --git a/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c b/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/sdhci.c
@@ -1021,2 +1028,3 @@
 	cfg->b_max = CONFIG_SYS_MMC_MAX_BLK_COUNT;
+	cfg->auto_stop = host->v4_mode;
 
